<title>UK: Aspen sells insurance stake for 8.25 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Aspen sells insurance stake for 8.25 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Aspen Communications said on Monday it had agreed to sell its interest in Aspen Insurance Services Plc (AIS) held through AIS Holdings to Fortis (UK) Limited for 8.25 million stg.</p>
<p>It said net assets would increase by around 2.9 million stg while the net impact on the profit and loss account would be an exceptional charge of around 0.2 million stg.</p>
<p>AIS is a direct insurance sales business and sells household, motor and other products primarily to customers over 55 years old.</p>
<p>AIS had some 71,000 policies at December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Aspen said it had warranted Fortis that AIS's pretax loss was 0.4 million stg for the year to December 31, 1996 with turnover of 2.3 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
